          "heading": "Argentina, Uruguay, Chile and Brazil submit joint 2035 World Cup bid",
          "body": "Argentina is leading a joint bid with Uruguay, Chile and Brazil to host the 2035 Rugby World Cup, a push reported on 6 October. Union president Félix Páez Molina called it \"a very important step for Argentine rugby and for the entire region\". Eight Argentine grounds, from Buenos Aires' Monumental to Rosario's Gigante de Arroyito, feature in the proposal. World Rugby will announce its venues in November 2027."
