          "kicker": "Eligibility row",
          "heading": "Hajime Shoji's League One reverses plan to treat naturalised players as foreigners",
          "body": "In late August, League One backtracked on registration rules that would have treated some naturalised players as foreigners despite their Japanese passports. The league granted an exception for players who had acquired or applied for citizenship by May 2025, after legal challenges and a fierce backlash. Managing Executive Director Hajime Shoji admitted: \"We lacked communication with players who would be adversely affected by the changes.\" The wider system was designed to cut places for foreign-born players eligible to represent Japan."
